"Some places know fission magic, and the legacy holders keep a monopoly on it."
"Fission has been a caustic secret since the Ending of Magic."
"Most Questors would kill anyone who spreads fission knowledge, some for merely knowing it."
"Dalo's spell is fusion: it fuses deuterium with hydrogen, and its radiation sickens watchers."
"Nuclear magic is likely Esebus's grand Insight, enchanted into its flying battlesuits."
"The Esebus nuclear spell sets off small fission in rare heavy metals in the rock it hits."
"Esebus's nuclear spells have turned mountains into fields of rubble and glass."
"Light mana can steer gamma rays, electromagnetic shields stop alpha and beta, force stops neutrons."
"Later, Nathan teaches Stella fusion, fission, E=mc2 and binding energy as one Insight."
"Nathan makes the Heirs swear never to share or write down the nuclear Insight."
"Stella swears on her magic to use nuclear spells only on the mightiest foes."
"Stella's fusion Insight grants her no new mana type; it is not deep enough."
"Later, Stella's nuke spell is fed jars of deuterium-rich hydrogen, shells of force around a core."
"The nuke spell uses radiation shielding, a reaction chamber and boosting wizardry."
"The nuke spell uses about six mana types and detonates when a fragile force shell breaks."
"Any decent mage who knows the danger could stop a nuke spell from going off."
"Later, Stella's nuke spell can delete square miles, and she can steer its blast in an arc."
"A full-scale nuke spell would be visible from the far side of Davrar."
"Nuke spells can carry failsafes that cancel them if tampered with."
"Stella knows a trick to survive her own nuke, which fails if the nuke is overcharged."
"Later, Stella fires four nukes at the Helmaris blight city and levels its outer half."
"Later, Stella casts thirteen fusion spells as a nuclear walking barrage on the Aleph fortress."
"Years later, the Bloc plans atomic spells against Dawn's Concord and loses."
